{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794739198,"nonce":"Mrf0m5L4ah3r6c5lobZikSHj/kA=","message":"Cause found, fix in the working tree (not committed).\n\nwgpu 26's Surface::configure waits for the GPU and returns GpuWaitTimeout (\"Failed to wait for GPU to come idle\") when, after the wait, the queue still lists a submission as in flight. On the Pixel 10 Pro (Vulkan, wgpu-hal uses a timeline semaphore as the fence) that check races the driver: vkWaitSemaphores returns success for submission 3, and the vkGetSemaphoreCounterValue that follows reads 2. Read again straight afterwards (no delay) it reads 3. Seen in three crashes with wgpu-core instrumented through a patch copy: wait idx 3, wait result Ok(true), finished 2, queue not empty, then a re-read of 3 at 0, 1, 2, 5 and 10 ms.\n\nWhy start-up: the first frame is submitted, then Android's WindowResized arrives about 2 ms later with the size the surface was already configured at, and the runner reconfigures. The wait blocks on that frame, which is when the late counter value is visible. It is a driver inconsistency, so it can happen at any reconfigure while a frame is in flight (resume, rotation, Lost/Outdated, suboptimal), not only the first.\n\nExample app, cold start by `am start` after `am force-stop`: 11 aborts in 40 starts without the fix, 0 in 60 with it. The bench build crashed 1 in 10 earlier.\n\nFix: crates/blinc_app/src/android.rs `configure_surface` polls the device with PollType::Wait, retrying up to 8 times 1 ms apart until the queue reports empty, then configures; all four configure calls in the runner use it. A late value makes poll return Timeout, which is retried instead of aborting.\n\nNot done: the same-size WindowResized right after the first configure still reconfigures once, which costs a wait on the first frame; wgpu itself could treat this case as a retry (upstream, not filed).","files":null}]}